shlytics, the crash occurs while ExoPlayer releases itself, most likely when finishig an Activity. We weren't able to reproduce it, as it occurrs on devices we don't have.\r\n\r\n### [REQUIRED] Reproduction steps\r\nWe don't have any details about it yet, as Crashlytics log is all we have right now. \r\nIt most likely occurrs after calling `SimpleExoPlayer#release()` on one of devices mentioned at the bottom of the page.\r\n\r\n### [REQUIRED] A full bug report captured from the device\r\n```\r\nFatal Exception: java.lang.NullPointerException\r\nAttempt to invoke interface method 'void com.google.android.exoplayer2.drm.DrmSessionManager.release()' on a null object reference\r\ncom.google.android.exoplayer2.source.dash.DashMediaSource.releaseSourceInternal (DashMediaSource.java:730)\r\ncom.google.android.exoplayer2.source.BaseMediaSource.releaseSource (BaseMediaSource.java:186)\r\ncom.google.android.exoplayer2.ExoPlayerImplInternal.resetInternal (ExoPlayerImplInternal.java:957)\r\ncom.google.android.exoplayer2.ExoPlayerImplInternal.stopInternal (ExoPlayerImplInternal.java:850)\r\ncom.google.android.exoplayer2.ExoPlayerImplInternal.handleMessage (ExoPlayerImplInternal.java:402)\r\nandroid.os.Handler.dispatchMessage (Handler.java:98)\r\nandroid.os.Looper.loop (Looper.java:148)\r\nandroid.os.HandlerThread.run (HandlerThread.java:61)\r\n```\r\n### [REQUIRED] Version of ExoPlayer being used\r\n`2.11.1`\r\n\r\n### [REQUIRED] Device(s) and version(s) of Android being used\r\nDevices: OnePlus One, OnePlus5, Intel T2101L2B1C, Blackview BV7000, rockchip X99.02.3.01.d32, Xiaomi MIX, Nubia NX531J, JSR Innos_D6000\r\nAndroid Versions: 5.1, 5.1.1, 6.0.1, 7.0, 7.1.2, 10","closed_by":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url